    <section class="finding">
      <h3>F3 — One template, many brands</h3>
      <blockquote><u>“I can answer any of your questions about our business, culture, team and more”</u></blockquote>
      <p>That sentence appears character-identical in <strong>15 of the 32</strong> tested deployments — McDonald's, Chipotle, 7-Eleven, Nestlé, Ace Hardware, Johnson Controls, Supercuts, Marriott, Crocs, FedEx, Whole Foods, and in Phase 5: UOB, BOK Financial, Fontainebleau Las Vegas, and Essentia Health (which carries it in the greeting <em>and</em> at question F) — in sessions where it answered none of them. A shorter form of the same claim appears in at least 10. Phase 5 also documented a second shared sentence, a deflection: <u>“Job responsibilities will vary depending on the job role. Please see the job listing associated with the desired role for details”</u> — used repeatedly by Essentia Health's Olivia and UOB's Jonus.</p>
      <figure class="shot">
        <a class="shot-link" href="/images/08-t-mobile-cass-claim-and-deflection.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="View full size — original capture"><img src="/images/08-t-mobile-cass-claim-and-deflection.jpg" alt="Browser capture of T-Mobile's CASS making the same question-answering claim, then deflecting a request to explain the role to the job description" /></a>
        <figcaption>T-Mobile's “CASS” makes the identical claim — then, asked to explain the role, deflects to the job description: “you will find the job responsibilities listed.” Browser capture from the test session, November 6, 2026.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="finding">
      <h3>F4 — False statements about real jobs</h3>
      <p>Compass Group's Olivia, launched from a live Cook (Seasonal) posting, stated:</p>
      <blockquote><u>“We don't currently have any positions open.”</u></blockquote>
