        <figcaption>The denial, in session: asked about the live Cook (Seasonal) role after declining to share a name, Olivia says no positions are open — then asks for the name again. Browser capture from the test session, November 6, 2026.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>Phase 5 added the cleanest instance yet. BOK Financial's Olivia, launched from a live Wealth Advisor posting in Topeka, Kansas, answered the question about that role with: <u>“We don't currently have any Wealth Advisor positions open in Scarborough, ON, CA”</u> — a false denial of the posting on screen, compounded by the location substitution below. In <strong>five deployments</strong> the assistant answered against the wrong location — Toronto, Ontario (the test session's geolocation) for US postings: Sodexo, Johnson Controls, Gap, Burlington, whose Allison also denied that Toronto openings existed in answer to a question about a Tyler, Texas posting, and BOK Financial.</p>
