    <section class="finding">
      <h3>F6 — Almost no way out</h3>
      <p>In <strong>only 5 of the 32</strong> deployments did the assistant point to a real application-form route (Compass Group, Marriott, Accenture; Phase 5 added BOK Financial and Essentia Health). No deployment, in any session, <strong>offered a human</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <h2 class="sec">The passes</h2>
    <p>Compass Group, question E. Asked for a regular form instead of the chatbot, Olivia pointed to the Apply Now button on the page. <strong>The audit's first pass, in 191 tests</strong> — at the same deployment that produced F4's false denial. The full session is <a href="/transcripts/compass-group-olivia-2026-11-06/">in the vault</a>.</p>
    <p>Phase 5 (November 7) added two more — the same question, the same shape: <strong>BOK Financial</strong> and <strong>Essentia Health</strong> each pointed to the posting's own Apply route. <strong>Three passes in 247 tests</strong>, every one of them question E, every one of them the assistant pointing at the form it was standing in front of. Sessions: <a href="/transcripts/bok-financial-olivia-2026-11-07/">BOK Financial</a> · <a href="/transcripts/essentia-health-olivia-2026-11-07/">Essentia Health</a>.</p>
